      },
      "37": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "CREATING THE SHAPE\n\nThe concept of the patch is that we have a solid color to fill the screen from which we subtract a shape, creating a border.\n\nFirst we create three different shapes: a rectangle, circle and a rhombus.\nWe have a Float In (renamed to Thickness), running from 0 to 1.\nThe 1-x node is used to flip the value. Instead of running from 0 to 1, we have a value running from 1 to 0.\n\nThe value is sent to a couple of Multiply nodes that are tuned just right so that they can go from a small dot to a screen filling shape.\n\nFinally we send the shapes to a Switch node controlled by a Choice In node (that we renamed to Type). This allows the user to switch between the three modes.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 852.7374877929688,
          "width": 1644.972412109375,
          "x": -1932.9849853515625,
          "y": 37.806488037109375
