      "52": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "TEXTURE SUBTRACTION\n\nHere we render the shape to a texture with a user defined color.\nWe also create a solid color texture with the same color as the shape.\nNext, we subtract the rendered shape from the solid color and we end up with a border.\n\nA color and a pixel are similar in a way that they both hold 4 values: red, green, blue and alpha.\n\nWhat is happening in the subtract node is that we evaluate the color value of each pixel on the left and subtract the value on the right from it. \nBecause the color of our shape and the color of the solid are the same, the result of the subtraction is always Float4(0,0,0,0), in other words: transparent.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 754.8699340820312,
          "width": 1054.4512939453125,
          "x": -256.9962158203125,
          "y": 37.76435089111328
        },
